                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we define the object as an option?\n\nThe object path seems to vary by system \u2014 I don\u2019t see it defined in the system inventory YAML.\n\nShould we use the interface instead?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "> Can we define the object as an option?\n\nI don't think I follow, because that's what I'm doing.  that inventory/system value is just the default but someone can change it if they want.\n\nIf I had it go find the Item.System object to get the path instead, then that would add in a new prereq, that even if the position was known before the Item.System interface was present, phosphor-logging couldn't use it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry for confusion.\n\n> find the Item.System object\n\nYes, I am not sure whether the defining a object path as argument is allowed or is it ok? so checking whether we could define a argument to pass the interface and use mapper to get the object path.\n\n> the position was known before the Item.System interface was present, phosphor-logging couldn't use it.\n\nOK"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 68,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "> Yes, I am not sure whether the defining a object path as argument is allowed or is it ok?\n\nIt's done in other places, like here: https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-state-manager/blob/master/meson.options#L18"
                }
            ],
